cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, its attack register or its report, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "quis-custodiet: benchmark integrity for AI code optimization"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered, adversarially tested benchmark for AI code optimization,
  with isolated measurement, documented attack limits, and a negative pilot
  result. The task is speeding up tomli's TOML parser (_parser.py, commit
  5a77b12); the judge (v5) removes capabilities from the candidate and is
  tested against a register of 24 known attacks, each first run on a
  vulnerable reference. The pre-registered pilot (9 runs, 3 models) ended in
  a scientific STOP.
authors:
